cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Below zero: scoring rules that price being wrong"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gonzalez
    given-names: Ramon
repository-code: "https://github.com/ramongonzalez12/there-should-be-a-cost-to-guessing"
url: "https://ramongonzalez.com/cost-to-guessing/"
abstract: >-
  Across 1,089,024 published model responses spanning 104 models and 36
  benchmarks, 0.69% contain any admission of not knowing and 0.25% state a
  probability. This repository documents that census, proposes a strictly proper
  scoring rule with a priced abstention threshold, and provides a pre-registered
  experiment testing whether announcing the rule to the model changes its
  behaviour.
keywords:
  - language models
  - evaluation
  - calibration
  - proper scoring rules
  - abstention
license: MIT
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Below zero: essay graded responses, tables, and figure data"
    authors:
      - family-names: Gonzalez
        given-names: Ramon
    abstract: >-
      Graded responses of 77 language models to 800 questions from eight
      benchmarks under four prompts (181,628 rows, no question text), with the
      tables, per-figure CSVs, and key numbers of the essay, rebuildable with no
      API key.
    repository: "https://github.com/ramongonzalez12/there-should-be-a-cost-to-guessing"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: "data/essay/ in the repository"
